# KEBU OPPORTUNITY OS

Opportunity OS is an **AI-powered Opportunity Operating System** — not a blog, not a static article list, not a brochure.

**Mission:** Help African entrepreneurs answer (1) What should I build? (2) How do I build it? Every opportunity should connect toward Kebu’s business builder.

## Navigation pillars (build slice-by-slice)

Countries · Industries · Resources · Imports · Exports · Trade · Manufacturing · Agriculture · Technology · Tourism · Infrastructure · Government Programs · Grants · Startup Ecosystem · Entrepreneur Stories · Company Case Studies · Opportunity Explorer · Opportunity AI · Build This Business

## Trust labels (mandatory)

Always separate:

- **Verified** public information
- **Estimated**
- **AI-generated** opportunity analysis
- **Requires validation**

Never present AI assumptions as verified facts.

## Data & CMS

Normalized entities (countries, industries, resources, commodities, imports/exports, opportunities, case studies, sources, confidence…). Content must be DB/CMS-backed — **not hard-coded production pages**. Admin CMS for publish/version/archive (when that slice is assigned).

## Build integration (later slices)

“Build This Business” creates drafts only (business, brand, website, optional store, roadmap, checklist, Kebu ID draft, readiness) — never auto-publish.

## Security

Opportunity catalog is public unless marked otherwise. Never leak private business data. Admin actions require RBAC.

## Slice order (do not skip)

1 Country Explorer → 2 Industry → 3 Resource → 4 Import → 5 Export → 6 Opportunity Explorer → 7 Entrepreneur Stories → 8 Case Studies → 9 Opportunity AI → 10 Build This Business

A static content-only page is **not** a completed slice. Finish and verify one vertical path before the next.
